10.4 Choosing a variance structure
A variance function should be considered when residual spread changes systematically across fitted values or time.
Selection should consider:

residual-versus-fitted plots;
normalized residuals;
information criteria;
parameter stability;
biological plausibility.

A lower AIC alone is insufficient if the fitted variance structure produces unstable parameters or implausible trajectories.

